# Static-target portability probe for the anyparse CORE — see
# docs/testing.md § "The core stays target-independent".
#
# Deliberately NOT the test runner: the suite calls js.node directly and is
# js-only. This builds parser + writer + every builtin check for --jvm, with
# no -lib hxnodejs and no stubs, so a bare `import js.node.…` or a structure
# that only unifies under a laxer typer fails here instead of silently.
#
# A bare hxml-include line and every relative path inside an hxml resolve
# against the CWD, so run this from the repo root:
#   haxe tools/jvm-portability.hxml && java -jar bin/jvm-portability.jar
#
# Running it needs a JVM; anyparse itself never does.
-cp src
-cp tools
-main JvmPortability
# Mirrors bin/apq-js-common.hxml so the probe exercises the shipped codegen.
-D analyzer-optimize
--jvm bin/jvm-portability.jar
